eries of drops that makes up Lower Initiation.  The big hole is just out of frame to the right.","caption":"Lower Initiation","poi_name":"Lower Initiation","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8304","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8304"}},{"id":"8182","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7094","description":"This is one of those Indian rock fish stopper things....Hope the Native American on BT don't get offended.....","caption":"Taylor~3","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Josh Wolverton","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8182","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8182"}},{"id":"8180","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7095","description":"Ozark Society trip.........Not sure if there is anything wrong with the pic, but the BT general forum will be the judge of that..............","caption":"Taylor River~1","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Josh Wolverton","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8180","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8180"}},{"id":"8307","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"This is looking downstream at the top of Slot, the big rocks in the other picture are just out of frame on the left.","caption":"Slot (2)","poi_name":"Slot","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8307","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8307"}},{"id":"8310","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"This is the biggest of the man made fishing dams in the Middle Taylor section.  The proper line is through the last chute on the right.  The drop is about four feet.","caption":"Fishing Dam","poi_name":"unkown","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8310","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8310"}},{"id":"872380","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872381","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872380","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872380"}},{"id":"872378","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"872379","description":"Taylor River Access","caption":"No Tresspass","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/872378","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/872378"}},{"id":"8183","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7095","description":"Open boat action on the Taylor......Despite all of the potential controversy over there at boatertalk.com that was the best line in the rapid......we scouted it and everything...........","caption":"Taylor~4","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Josh Wolverton","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8183","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8183"}},{"id":"873910","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"873911","description":"","caption":"Colorado River Access","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/873910","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/873910"}},{"id":"8309","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"Some manky waves below Slot.","caption":"Lower Slot","poi_name":"Slot","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8309","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8309"}},{"id":"8181","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7095","description":"A little Duckie action.........Helmet, Pfd, Paddle (no leash), Well BT guys, don't guess anything wrong here unless it's the Duckie........:)","caption":"Taylor~2","poi_name":"","subject":"Phil Proctor","author":"Josh Wolverton","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8181","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8181"}},{"id":"8308","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"Looking upstream at the rocks that make up Slot.","caption":"Slot (3)","poi_name":"Slot","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8308","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8308"}},{"id":"8311","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"Looking up at the end of the Taylor River canyon.","caption":"Taylor River Canyon","poi_name":"n/a","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8311","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8311"}},{"id":"8312","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"Going over the rock on river right spins a raft really well.","caption":"Toilet Bowl","poi_name":"Toilet Bowl","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8312","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8312"}},{"id":"8313","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"Not the best picture, but the best line here is to go behind the big rock, then work back river left right after it and scoot through the goal posts.","caption":"The Goalposts","poi_name":"The Goalposts","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":"106140","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8313","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8313"}},{"id":"8306","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7767","description":"This is a nice looking Class IV just above the put in for the commercial trips.","caption":"Slot","poi_name":"Slot","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8306","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8306"}},{"id":"8303","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"This is the entrance to Initiation.","caption":"Upper Initiation","poi_name":"Upper Initiation","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8303","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8303"}},{"id":"8305","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7768","description":"This big hole makes up Middle Initiation.  It gets bigger and meaner as the water rises.","caption":"Middle Initiation","poi_name":"Middle Initiation","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8305","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8305"}},{"id":"889629","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892173","description":"Paddler Zach Allen kayaking through the Cataracts on the Taylor Park run. June 16, 2007","caption":"Zach Allen on the Cataracts 700 cfs","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Kit Davidson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/889629","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/889629"}}],"detail":{"id":"428","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"The Taylor River is stunning and beautiful with alpine scenery, a boulder-strewn course through the pines offering up whitewater at different levels.\n\nAnother great thing about the Taylor River is options:\n\nThe top reasonably boatable section, there are serious access problems above here, begins at Lottis Creek Campground.\n\nThe first rapid; Lottis Creek, appears immediately. It is a long Class IV boulder garden. Next comes several miles of rock gardens alternating with more placid sections. Todd's Slot is the best known drop on the river and is a technical Class IV / IV rapid. It is a bit complex and has killed so take a look at this rapid. Below Todd's Slot are miles of beautiful continuous Class III mountain water to the takeout by the south bank bridge right above Harmels resort. Below this bridge to Almont the river steadly decreases in gradient until it is a placid Class II stream where it meets the East River at Almont to form the Gunnison River. The top miles below Lottis Creek drop at about 80 FPM with the gradient steadly decreasing to 20 FPM at Almont.  This is a trophy trout stream with constant releases all summer to maintain the fishery. Watch for wood, especially given the fast pace of the water. The Taylor River is known for being woody, its Colorado.\n\nThe Taylor is a superb Beginner (near Almont), Intermediate (below Todd's slot) and Advanced (from Lottis Creek) river and **will have water when most everything else is dry**.\n\nFor best gauge see: The gauge below the dam:\n\n[https://waterdata.usgs.gov/co/nwis/dv/?site\\_no=09109000&PARAmeter\\_cd=00060](https://waterdata.usgs.gov/co/nwis/dv/?site_no=09109000&PARAmeter_cd=00060)\n\n\\[The one linked is at Almont which also includes Spring Creek, which comes in below the South Bank takeout.\\]","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"12","correlations":[{"reachID":"428","isPrimary":true,"correlationDeta